  "summary_en": "December 2020 update of Germany's national AI Strategy, backed by €5 billion through 2025. It prioritises AI talent, research, transfer to SMEs, a regulatory framework for trustworthy AI, sustainability and civil society. Embodied AI appears only in passing (autonomous driving, urban air mobility, Industry 4.0, care).",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Raises planned federal AI funding from €3bn to €5bn by 2025.",
   "Aims to establish 'AI Made in Europe' as a trademark of responsible, public-good-oriented AI.",
   "Expands quality infrastructure into a system for safe, secure and trustworthy AI, including standards and certification.",
   "Plans a central certification/conformity assessment body for AI used by security authorities.",
   "Reviews labour, social and other law for changes triggered by AI; develops an environmental impact assessment concept for AI."
